WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.820
Eczema is a common
skin disease

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.060
and there are plenty of drugs
on the market to combat it.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.500
But what about diet?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.140
Are there foods
that trigger eczema,

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.840
and can dietary changes
be used to treat it?

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.000
Watch to find out.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.259
"Best Foods to Avoid for Eczema &amp;
Exclusion Diets for Eczema"

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.720
Eczema, also known
as atopic dermatitis,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.300
is a chronic inflammatory
skin disease.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.540
In fact, it’s the leading cause
of healthy years of life lost

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.920
due to common skin diseases,
because it’s just so common,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.780
affecting up to
a fifth of us.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.520
And, it's not just
an itchy rash;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.980
it’s associated with
other diseases too.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.980
Yes, it can be itchy, exhausting,
and embarrassing,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.640
but in kids, it may
increase risk for ADHD,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.520
though that may just be
from the sleep deprivation.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.660
And, in adults, it may increase
the risk of major depression.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.720
And, it’s on the rise.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.640
There are drugs for it, of course;
there are always drugs.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.860
Steroids are the
first-line therapy,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.100
but then there are
immunosuppressants as well,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.140
with more in the
drug pipeline.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.260
You know the medical
profession is desperate

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.840
when they’re forced to go
back to the basics

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.360
and start applying
leeches to people.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.860
Previously, I talked about
the safety and efficacy

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.600
of other, more
natural treatments,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.640
but what about diet?

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.800
Our story begins in 1920, a year
doctors were realizing

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.140
how good this
oxygen stuff was,

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.940
though maybe not as good as
injecting people with mercury,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.560
but a researcher at Johns Hopkins
reported a number of cases

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.100
in which by omitting eggs, meat,
and milk from the diet,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.800
patients’ eczema improved.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.320
Who’s going to profit
off of that though?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.140
No wonder it took 58 years
before it was put to the test.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.380
Figuring eggs and milk
were the two foods

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.440
most likely involved in eczema,
they excluded them—

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.880
and chicken and beef,

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.360
since it may just be chicken and
cow proteins more generally,

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.000
in a randomized double-blind
controlled trial

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.120
swapping in soy milk
instead, and…

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.720
70% of the patients
improved.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.540
One person got worse on the no egg,
no chicken, no milk, no beef diet,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.540
but almost everyone
else got better.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.440
So, the researchers concluded
that for many kids,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.620
avoiding those foods may
induce a clinical improvement.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.680
And interestingly,
it didn’t seem to depend

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.340
on whether allergy tests showed
they were allergic to milk and eggs.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.700
Either way, they tended
to get better, regardless.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.420
You can do randomized double-blind
food challenges,

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.560
where you give kids with eczema
various foods in opaque capsules,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.780
like one with egg powder,
one with wheat powder, etc.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.280
Egg was found by far to be
the most offending food.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.940
For example, in this study, where
they just cut out the eggs,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.400
dramatic improvements
were documented

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.720
for both the amount of skin involvement
and the severity of the eczema lesions

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.000
after removing
eggs from the diet,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.280
but in about 90% of cases,
the mom had no idea

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.960
that eggs were
a problem.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.000
Why?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.820
Because it wasn’t like they were
eating scrambled eggs or something.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.880
Almost all the egg
exposure was hidden;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.260
they were exposed to hidden
egg products in packaged foods.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.900
So, they had no idea why their
eczema was so bad—

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.560
until this study, where they
removed all eggs

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.140
and egg products
from their diets.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.800
Eggs are evidently the
most frequent cause

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.420
of food sensitivity
in children.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.000
Out of hundreds of kids
with eczema tested,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.840
egg allergy was documented in about
two-thirds of those with sensitivities.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.500
In fact, a child having a blood
reaction to egg white proteins

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.420
appears to be one of the
best laboratory tests

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.600
for predicting future allergic
diseases in general.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.940
It appears to be the ovomucoid
protein within egg whites

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.880
that seems to be causing
most of the mischief.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.820
About 40% of kids with eczema
have some form of food allergy.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.560
And, the more food
allergies they have,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.660
the more likely it appears
they’re going to suffer

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.660
from eczema— and,
make it worse.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.940
Those who react to
cows’ milk protein

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.480
are significantly more likely
to suffer severe eczema,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.240
showing the important role
cows’ milk proteins may play

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.500
“in the induction and increased
severity of eczema in children.”

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.280
Often, parents switch from cows’
milk to goats’ milk,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.800
in an attempt to improve
their children’s eczema.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.800
But goats’ milk should never
be given to kids

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.940
with a cows’ milk allergy,

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.040
because they often cross-react
with one another,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.020
which has been confirmed with double-blind
placebo controlled food challenges.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.740
Ass milk, on the other hand,
is a different story.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.220
Switching kids to donkey
milk improved their eczema,

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:04.576
and, for that matter, horse’s
milk might, as well.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.100
The original randomized,
double-blind, controlled trial

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.260
of diet and eczema
found that cutting out

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.060
eggs, chicken, milk, and beef

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.580
significantly improved eczema in 70%

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.920
of the kids that
completed the study.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.380
Subsequent studies
found similar results,

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.880
though in this case,
for example,

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.100
it only seemed to work for
a quarter of the kids.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.920
But, bottom line,
out of 13 studies

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.480
on avoiding milk,
eggs, or both,

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.220
10 out 13 studies documented
overall clinical improvement.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.160
The economic burden
of eczema

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.680
caused by just regular
cows’ milk formula alone

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.260
may be hundreds of millions
of dollars a year,

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.380
though eggs appear to be worse,

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:49.980
in terms of predicting persistence
and severity of the disease.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.340
Sensitization to egg
white and cows’ milk

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.820
can occur even in breast-fed
infants though.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.860
So, presumably the source
of the exposure

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.840
is the passage of egg
and cow proteins

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.160
through the mother’s milk,

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.820
but you don’t know until
you put it to the test.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.120
New mothers were randomized
to cut out eggs,

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.340
cows’ milk, and fish
from their diet

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.440
during the first three months
of breastfeeding

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.860
after giving birth or to
continue their regular diet.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.960
And indeed, the
infants of mothers

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.400
who cut out the eggs,
milk, and fish

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.020
were significantly less likely
to have eczema by age 6 months,

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.260
though after that age, the
decreased rates of eczema

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.180
in the no eggs/milk
or fish group

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.520
were no longer
statistically significant.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.060
Follow those same kids
out to four years, though,

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.940
and those whose
moms cut out the eggs,

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.320
milk, and dairy for
just three months

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.720
while breast feeding
had significantly

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.420
lower eczema rates
even years later.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.740
Consuming that hypoallergenic
diet during breastfeeding

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:53.640
cut child eczema
rates in half.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.960
Eating more plant
foods may also help.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.060
The majority of fruit
and vegetable studies

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.520
suggest that higher consumption
by mothers during pregnancy,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.260
and children in
early life,

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.300
results in reductions
in asthma,

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.280
another allergic-
type disease.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:12.180
Maybe it’s the phenolic phytonutrients
in plants that are helping,

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.720
supported by evidence that
certain vegetarian diets

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.060
appear to alleviate
the severity

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.580
of skin diseases in
adults with eczema.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.280
Though if you look
at that citation,

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:27.720
it was a very
strange diet.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.540
They found striking
benefits in terms

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.040
of reducing the
severity of eczema,

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.860
and even 2 months after
they went off the diet,

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.080
they were still doing better
than when they started,

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.260
but the diet was
just vegetable juice,

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:45.240
brown rice, kelp, tofu,
tahini, and persimmon leaf tea,

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:48.900
and severely
calorie-restricted.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.980
And, just straight fasting
alone can improve eczema,

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.220
as can a strictly
plant-based diet,

00:07:56.220 --> 00:08:00.000
which is not so
surprising given the data

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.260
on children showing
how much better

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.360
they can do cutting
out eggs and dairy.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.780
In spite of these data,
dermatologists

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.400
and pediatricians have,
for many years,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.220
denied the role of
food in eczema,

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.160
even though as many as
80% of kids may benefit

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.020
cutting out milk
and/or eggs

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:20.340
regardless of what the
various allergy tests show.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.220
You can’t necessarily tell
if diet is going to help,

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.120
until you yourself put it
to the test in your own body.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.880
And, that’s what
parents are doing.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.000
They’re not waiting for
their pediatricians to catch up;

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.600
75% of parents with
eczema-stricken kids

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.180
have tried some form
of dietary exclusion,

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.280
most commonly cutting
out dairy and eggs,

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.980
though only about
40% of parents

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.900
who tried it feel
that it worked.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.420
But hey, why not
give it a try?

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:53.040
A typical recommendation you
see in the medical literature is,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.560
“Look, if you have a
child with some bad eczema,

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.300
and the drugs
aren’t working,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.540
then... why don’t you try
cutting out some foods?”

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.400
But, that seems
to me backwards.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.020
If foods are
contributing,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.120
why not treat
the cause

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.980
and eliminate the
offending foods,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.220
and then do the drugs
if diet isn’t enough.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.800
Now, there are some pretty
nutty eczema diets out there,

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.140
like the so-called
“few foods” diet,

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.380
excluding everything
except lamb, potatoes,

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.900
Rice Krispies, broccoli,
and pears.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.020
To my surprise, it was
actually put to the test—

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.420
I told you docs
were desperate!

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.420
But it failed to
show a benefit.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.880
Basically, if you don’t know
where to begin,

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.660
the simplest approach may be to
just cut out dairy and eggs

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.680
and see what happens.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.280
That’s a controversial
recommendation, though.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.200
Avoiding fish, beef,
eggs, and dairy

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.940
without medical
supervision?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.300
That might trigger
malnutrition-related pathology.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.860
What?!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.320
I checked out
that citation,

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.760
and it's just another article
making an unsupported claim.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:05.400
Now, if you exclude everything,
like 99% of your diet

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.480
is rice milk, well then, obviously,
that’s completely insufficient,

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.960
but for most parents,
the #1 thing they add

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.780
to their child’s diet for
eczema... is vegetables,

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.020
and the #1 thing they cut
down on is.... junk food,

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.940
and I don’t think
we have to worry,

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.441
about a junk
food deficiency.

